From e0f6aed637ddc21cc89473a63fc7f573590b68ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:35:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0125 -- re-derive src_pitch when the surface
 changes in place

fb_state is populated once, in CreateWindowFramebuffer, and every flush
in DOSVESA_UpdateWindowFramebuffer then trusts src_pitch, pixels and
pitches_match for the life of that framebuffer.

A mode-set that changes the surface geometry in place therefore leaves
each flush copying rows at the old stride. Every scanline lands short or
long by the pitch delta, so the picture shears progressively down the
frame rather than failing outright.

Observed rather than hypothesised: a Mach64 running UniVBE + LFB at
640x480 logs pitches_match=0 while fb_state still carries the pitch from
the mode it was created in. It is not live on the card-ROM banked path,
which is why it has survived this long -- the configuration that exposes
it is not the one most cells run, so every recent measurement has been
taken somewhere the defect is dormant.

A wholly-new surface with a different pointer is already handled: SDL
calls CreateWindowFramebuffer again and repopulates fb_state. This
covers the in-place case, which nothing else does.

Cost on the common path is one pointer dereference and one integer
compare per flush; the body runs only when the pitch has actually moved,
and it logs when it does, because a stride changing under a live
framebuffer is worth knowing about even once it is handled.

The anchor for this insertion is deliberately positional. The
instrumentation entry block it follows appears five times in this file,
so matching on that text alone would have placed the re-derivation into
four unrelated functions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
index dde73e0ed..5efba3c60 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
@@ -1344,6 +1344,41 @@ bool DOSVESA_UpdateWindowFramebuffer(SDL_VideoDevice *device, SDL_Window *window
     const Uint64 _instr_t_entry =
         _instr_enabled_cached ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
 
+    // DOSKUTSU patch 0125: re-derive the source pitch when the app surface
+    // changes under a live framebuffer.
+    //
+    // fb_state is populated once, in CreateWindowFramebuffer, and every
+    // flush below then trusts src_pitch / pixels / pitches_match for the
+    // life of that framebuffer. A mode-set that changes the surface
+    // geometry IN PLACE therefore leaves each flush copying rows at the old
+    // stride: every scanline lands short or long by the pitch delta and the
+    // picture shears progressively down the frame.
+    //
+    // Observed, not hypothesised: a Mach64 on UniVBE + LFB at 640x480 logs
+    // pitches_match=0 while fb_state still carries the pitch from the mode
+    // it was created in. It is NOT live on the card-ROM banked path, which
+    // is why it has survived -- the configuration that exposes it is not the
+    // one most cells run.
+    //
+    // A wholly-new surface (different pointer) is already covered: SDL calls
+    // CreateWindowFramebuffer again and repopulates fb_state. This handles
+    // the in-place case, which nothing else does.
+    //
+    // Cost on the common path is one dereference and one int compare; the
+    // body runs only when the pitch has actually moved.
+    if (fb_state.direct_fb && fb_state.surface &&
+        fb_state.surface->pitch != fb_state.src_pitch) {
+        const int _old_pitch   = fb_state.src_pitch;
+        fb_state.src_pitch     = fb_state.surface->pitch;
+        fb_state.pixels        = (Uint8 *)fb_state.surface->pixels;
+        fb_state.pitches_match = (fb_state.src_pitch == fb_state.vram_pitch);
+        DOSKUTSU_LC_LOG("src-pitch re-derived: %d -> %d (vram_pitch=%d "
+                        "pitches_match=%d) -- surface changed under a live "
+                        "framebuffer",
+                        _old_pitch, fb_state.src_pitch, fb_state.vram_pitch,
+                        (int)fb_state.pitches_match);
+    }
+
     // DOSKUTSU patch 0015 (Phase 9 wave 3, Fix B): fast-path timing
     // brackets. Wave-2 measurements showed real-Cirrus title flips at
     // 333-367 ms / 2.94 fps even with LFB engaged, ~325 ms unaccounted
